WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:11.790
While the size of Arctic sea ice has dropped by about 40 percent over 40 years, until recently, the size of the sea ice around Antarctica was slowly increasing.
40年来，北极海冰的面积减少了约40%，而南极洲周围的海冰面积直到不久前还一直在缓慢增加。

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:21.450
Then, after 2015, Antarctic ice extent fell from a record high to several record lows, losing an area as large as Greenland.
后来，2015年过后，南极海冰的范围从创纪录的高点下跌，多次跌至创纪录的低点，减少的面积有格陵兰岛那么大。

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:26.220
Some research has suggested that higher air temperatures may be the cause.
有研究提出，原因可能在于气温升高。

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:32.100
However, two new studies show that ocean warming played a bigger role in this dramatic change.
然而，两项新研究表明，在这一剧烈变化中，海洋变暖起了更大的作用。

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:41.930
As part of global ocean circulation, warm saltwater moves southward from the tropics and circles Antarctica 200 metres below the surface.
作为全球海洋环流的一部分，温暖的咸水从热带向南流去，并在海面以下200米处环绕南极洲。

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:52.110
But temperature and saltiness records of the past 20 years suggest that this warm deep saltwater has been rising towards the surface, where it can melt sea ice.
但过去20年的温度和盐度记录表明，这股温暖的深层咸水一直在朝海面上升，到了海面就能使海冰融化。

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:56.630
Antarctica is encircled by a belt of strong winds and storms.
南极洲四周环绕着一条由强风和风暴构成的地带。

00:00:57.430 --> 00:01:08.280
Climate change has pushed this storm belt southward, bringing more rain and snow into the sea ice area, according to a study by Earle Wilson and other researchers at Stanford University.
据斯坦福大学的厄尔·威尔逊和其他研究人员所做的一项研究，气候变化已经使这条风暴带向南推移，给海冰区域带来了更多雨雪。

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:19.520
The rain and snow create a layer of fresh surface water that better protects the bottom of the sea ice from warm deep saltwater, allowing it to grow to its 2014 record high.
这些雨雪形成了一层表层淡水，能更好地保护海冰底部不受温暖的深层咸水影响，使海冰得以增长到2014年创纪录的高点。

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:24.010
But the same southward-moving storm belt also brings stronger winds.
但同样是这条向南移动的风暴带，也带来了更强的风。

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:27.320
These winds blow surface water and ice forward.
这些风把表层水和冰向前吹去。

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:32.820
As this happens, warm deep saltwater rises up to fill the empty space.
这时，温暖的深层咸水就会上升，填补空出来的空间。

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:45.190
Between 2014 and 2016, this wind-driven rising began to get the upper hand against the protective layer of increased rain and snow, and sea ice began to melt away.
2014年至2016年间，这种由风驱动的上升作用在与雨雪增多所形成的保护层的较量中开始占据上风，海冰开始融化消失。

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:55.820
When the researchers input the recorded ocean data into a computer model, it projected that sea ice would grow and then become smaller, as it did in the real world.
研究人员把记录下来的海洋数据输入计算机模型后，模型预测海冰会先增长、然后变小，就像现实世界中发生的那样。

00:01:56.620 --> 00:02:02.520
The researchers plan to study and model other things, which also likely play roles throughout Antarctica.
研究人员计划研究其他因素并为它们建立模型，这些因素很可能也在整个南极洲发挥着作用。

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:10.020
Examples include changes in sea ice movement and increases in ocean mixing resulting from more storms.
举例来说，这些因素包括海冰运动的变化，以及风暴增多所导致的海洋混合增强。

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:17.950
By studying the ocean data, they hope to build a model to project changes in Antarctic sea ice in the years to come.
他们希望通过研究这些海洋数据，建立一个模型，来预测今后几年南极海冰的变化。
